# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# Windows editors silently rewrite whole files from LF to CRLF on save. Git then
# reports every line as changed even though nothing did — 420 lines of noise in a
# diff that should have been empty. `text=auto` tells Git to store LF in the
# repository and check files out in whatever form the platform prefers, so that
# never reaches a commit.
#
# If a file still shows a whole-file diff after this, run:
#     git add --renormalize .
* text=auto

# Explicit for the file types this site is built from, so intent is obvious.
*.html   text
*.css    text
*.js     text
*.json   text
*.md     text
*.csv    text
*.py     text
*.yml    text

# Binary assets — Git must never rewrite bytes inside these.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.svg    text
*.mp4    binary
*.docx   binary
*.pdf    binary
